        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dced713a-b01e-5d5c-8e51-0efcf9a4b86f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Princess Johanna of Hesse and by Rhine, Georg Donatus, Princess Cecilie, Ludwig, Alexander, Eleonore\n- Events: Sabena OO-AUB Ostend crash, family wedding in London\n- Places: Ostend, Stene Airport, London\n\nFacts:\n- Princess Johanna Marina Eleonore of Hesse and by Rhine was born on 20 September 1936 as the third child and only daughter of Georg Donatus, Hereditary Grand Duke of Hesse, and Princess Cecilie of Greece and Denmark.\n- Princess Johanna of Hesse and by Rhine was orphaned at the age of fourteen months when her parents, her older brothers Ludwig and Alexander, and her paternal grandmother Eleonore were killed in a plane crash while traveling to a family wedding in London.\n- At Ostend, conditions were only slightly better, but the Sabena OO-AUB aircraft hit a factory chimney while circling to land at Stene Airport.\n- Princess Johanna of Hesse and by Rhine died on 14 June 1939.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
